@@s001 Assignments and oral feedback
@@s002 <span>Exam</span>
@@s003 Assignments and oral feedback
@@s004 The assignments are the ticket to the exam: <b>6 assignments</b>, of which <b>5 approved</b> are needed. They are handed in as a group on Monday at 07:59 and discussed orally with a TA. Here are the official rules and the status of your group.
@@s005 The rules in brief
@@s006 Groups
@@s007 2–3 people (Group Selection on LearnIT)
@@s008 What
@@s009 each assignment = solutions to <b>two</b> sets of weekly exercises
@@s010 Deadline
@@s011 <b>Monday at 07:59</b>, before the lecture
@@s012 How
@@s013 link to the repo on <code>github.itu.dk</code> in the LearnIT form
@@s014 Who hands in
@@s015 one member for the whole group; the grade is individual
@@s016 To be approved
@@s017 <b>all</b> the correct mandatory exercises; the mandatory code <b>must compile and run</b>
@@s018 Challenging
@@s019 not needed for approval; needed for high grades
@@s020 Tools
@@s021 Java 25, Gradle 9.6.1
@@s022 The code must run
@@s023 From the week 1 sheet: "Code that is close to correct, but that does not compile and run will not be accepted". It applies to the mandatory exercises.
@@s024 The repository
@@s025 In the repo only files linked to the delivery, with this structure.
@@s026 The written answers go in the files <code>textual_answers_exercisesNN.md</code>.
@@s027 <b>One branch only.</b> The repo must be <b>public</b> (lecture 1 slides).
@@s028 <b>Do not modify</b> the handed-in files after the delivery. To keep working on them: copy the files or make a fork.
@@s029 In the LearnIT form: group name, full names and GitHub usernames of everyone. Check that <code>git clone &lt;url&gt;</code> works.
@@s030 Oral feedback
@@s031 Slot of <b>40 minutes</b> with a TA or a teacher, booked on the LearnIT Organizer. <b>Every member</b> signs up for the same slot. At most 5 people per slot: at most two groups.
@@s032 The slot is <b>recurring</b>: same day and time in all the feedback weeks, <b>37, 39, 41, 44, 46, 49</b>.
@@s033 In person at the ITU. The TA books the room.
@@s034 Keep the project ready to project or share: you are asked to <b>explain and run</b> part of the code.
@@s035 All members must take part and be able to discuss <b>all</b> the exercises, not only those they wrote.
@@s036 Review the answers shortly before: you wrote them days ago.
@@s037 Why it matters for the exam
@@s038 The feedback serves to "uncover misunderstandings" and to train "discussing course material". It is the same exercise as the final oral. You can also bring course topics that are not clear to you.
